drm/esp32s31: say which buffer scanout actually reads

The diagnostic printed "from plane fb" whenever a client had a framebuffer at
all - `(plane_state && plane_state->fb)` - which is true in every case where
scanout is really the private compositing buffer. So it reported

    scaling: scanout buffer 768000 bytes at 0x50800000     <- private buffer
    enable scanout at 0x50800000, ... from plane fb        <- same address

and the label is simply wrong. That cost an afternoon: if the panel really were
scanning out the client's own buffer, then the per-frame damage copy into the
private one would be writing to memory nobody reads, and removing it would be
free. It is not free - esp32s31_lcd_composite() returns true unconditionally
because this DMA engine cannot be retargeted mid-session (-ENXIO), so the copy
is how content reaches the panel at all. The visible cursor was the proof: it
is composited into the private buffer, and it appears.

Report the buffer that feeds the DMA instead, by comparing against scan_phys.

Cosmetic - no functional change - so it is not flashed on its own; it lands
with the next kernel build.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/espressif/esp32s31-lcd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/espressif/esp32s31-lcd.c
@@ -1347,9 +1347,21 @@
 	       lcd->base + LCD_MISC_REG);
 
 	lcd->dbg_scanout_addr = fb_addr;
+	/*
+	 * Report which buffer actually feeds the DMA, not merely whether a
+	 * plane framebuffer exists.
+	 *
+	 * The old test was `plane_state && plane_state->fb`, which is true
+	 * whenever a client has a framebuffer at all - including every case
+	 * where scanout is really the private compositing buffer. It therefore
+	 * printed "from plane fb" while the DMA read scan_phys, and cost an
+	 * afternoon chasing a copy that looked redundant: if the panel really
+	 * were scanning out the client's buffer, the per-frame damage copy into
+	 * the private one would be writing to memory nobody reads. It is not.
+	 */
 	drm_info(&lcd->drm, "diag: enable scanout at %pad, %zu bytes, from %s\n",
 		 &fb_addr, fb_bytes,
-		 (plane_state && plane_state->fb) ? "plane fb" : "reserved fb");
+		 (fb_addr == lcd->scan_phys) ? "private buffer" : "plane fb");
 
 	ret = esp32s31_lcd_start_scanout(lcd, fb_addr, fb_bytes);
 	if (ret) {
